  "notes": "{萌|も}える has both a traditional meaning (to sprout) and a modern slang meaning (to feel passion).\n\nMEANINGS:\n1. Traditional: for plants to bud or sprout in spring\n2. Slang: to feel strong affection/enthusiasm, especially for anime characters\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {草木|くさき}が{萌|も}える: plants sprout\n- {萌黄色|もえぎいろ}: fresh green color (of new leaves)\n- このキャラに{萌|も}える: to feel passion for this character\n- {萌|も}え{絵|え}: moe-style illustration\n\nHOMOPHONE (different kanji):\n- {燃|も}える: to burn (fire)\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nThe slang {萌|も}え originated in otaku culture and expresses affection for fictional characters.",
